  <h2 id="introduction">Introduction</h2>
  <p>Chairs are part of the Furniture system used in the restaurant dining area. This category explains how chairs relate to Tables, customer space, and the wider layout.</p>

  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>The Chairs page is a category entry rather than a list of individual chair articles. Use it to understand where chairs belong in Furniture navigation and to continue into the Tables directory or Restaurant Layout Guide.</p>

  <h2 id="how-chairs-work">How Chairs Work</h2>
  <p>Chairs help establish where the customer area begins and how it is arranged around tables. A clear chair arrangement also makes the boundary between dining space, movement paths, and work areas easier to recognize.</p>

  <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
  <p>Plan chairs together with the surrounding tables and the space players use during service. Adjust their placement when the dining area becomes difficult to navigate or understand.</p>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Keep chairs grouped with the dining area they belong to.</li>
    <li>Leave clear paths between customer seating and restaurant work areas.</li>
    <li>Review the complete room after moving part of the seating arrangement.</li>
    <li>Use the Tables directory and Restaurant Layout Guide for connected planning information.</li>
  </ul>
</ContentPage>
